    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d75">

                <pb facs="0130" n="864" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg864"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Willis to Mr. Adee.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Abstract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Honolulu</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-09-04"><hi rendition="#italic">September 4, 1895</hi></date>.
                        (Received Sept. 18.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 133.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Government has pardoned 44 political
                    prisoners connected with the recent uprising. All of these are Hawaiians or
                    half-castes. <pb facs="0131" n="865" xml:id="pg865"/> Of these, the principal
                    are Jonah C. Kalanianaole (“Prince Cupid”); Carl Widemann, son of Hon. H. A.
                    Widemann, late commissioner to Washington of the ex-Queen, and the four Lane
                    brothers.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Albert S. Willis.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
